// E0507: a C++ header in a run that did not declare C++ mode.
// This file should FAIL to transpile with E0507.
//
// Issue #1319: C++ mode is declared (config `cppRequired` / --cpp), never
// discovered. Reading someone else's header used to switch the output language
// silently; it now says so and stops.
//
// `external-status.h` is the negative control: a pure C header included right
// beside the C++ one. A check that rejected every include would name it, and
// the .expected.error names only the .hpp -- so this fixture fails on
// over-enforcement as well as on under-enforcement.
#include "external-status.h"
#include "external-cpp-type.hpp"

void main() {}
